comb-experiment
===============

The code in this repository is MIT licensed - see LICENSE. That licence
covers the code in this repository and nothing else.

flysim.py, mushroom.py, envcfg.py and build_graph.py are carried over from
fruitflydev/flycoinrh (MIT), an unrelated project that used the same
connectome to drive a browser toward token launches. This fork keeps only
the LIF simulator and the mushroom-body learning rule, drops everything
related to wallets, providers and live signing, and adds a honeybee-dance
skin on top (antenna.py, dance.py, hive.py, roam_hive.py, web/).

The connectome is not ours to license. The male Drosophila CNS dataset
(FlyEM male CNS v1.0) is (c) HHMI Janelia FlyEM, the Cambridge Connectomics
Group and Google Research, released under CC-BY 4.0, and it stays under
CC-BY wherever it goes. If you fork this, keep that attribution. Simulation
methodology after Shiu et al. 2024 (Nature).

Apis mellifera facts cited in this project - antennal-lobe glomerulus count
on the order of 160-166 (Galizia lab honeybee AL atlas), the waggle dance's
angle/duration/vigor encoding (von Frisch; Seeley 1995), the dorsal-rim
polarization compass (Rossel & Wehner 1984) - are cited for the modelling
choices in dance.py and antenna.py's docstrings, not claimed as measured
from any EM data. There is no public, complete Apis mellifera connectome.
Nothing in this repository claims otherwise - see README.md, first line.

record.py's capture mechanics (headless Chromium, record_video_dir, webm ->
mp4) are carried over from flycoinrh's own record.py (MIT).

No part of this repository is financial advice, and no part of it mints,
holds, or signs for anything. $COMB is a display ticker with no on-chain
existence anywhere in this codebase.
